# ── Grain Conference Intelligence — environment variables ──────────────────
# Nothing below is required to run the app. Copy this file to .env.local
# only if you want to set server-side defaults. Reps can also (and by
# default, DO) enter their own API keys directly in the app's Settings page —
# those are kept in the browser only (localStorage) and are sent per-request
# to the small server proxies in app/api/, never written to disk or to a
# database. No key is ever hardcoded in this source.

# ── Shared, persistent storage (recommended for real team use) ─────────────
# Without these two, the app automatically falls back to a local JSON file
# (great for local dev and for a quick demo) — see lib/db.ts. For a real
# team deployment where every rep should see the same conferences/leads,
# create a free Upstash Redis database (2 minutes, no credit card, at
# upstash.com — or add the "Upstash" integration from the Vercel
# Marketplace, which sets these two variables for you automatically) and
# paste its REST URL/token here.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Optional server-side fallback keys ──────────────────────────────────────
# Only useful if you'd rather hardcode a shared team key as a deployment
# default instead of having each rep paste their own in Settings. Leave
# blank to require reps to configure their own key in Settings (recommended
# per the assignment's "configurable by the user" constraint).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
HUBSPOT_PRIVATE_APP_TOKEN=
